{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Brick.</b> Derived from לבנים. And although the combination with a mem is feminine, like נשים and פלגשים — now they burned the bricks until they held fast, and this is the strong construction that does not dissolve in water or in fire." "And they had brick for stone. Instead of stone." "<b>And the mortar.</b> Instead of clay. And its meaning is as it sounds in the language of Ishmael. And these builders of the tower were not fools, that they would intend to ascend to the heavens, nor did they fear the flood, for Noah and his sons — to whom HaShem swore — were there, and all were subject to their authority, for they were their children. Now Scripture disclosed their intent and the conclusion of their thought: to build a great city for their dwelling and to build a high tower to be for them a sign and a name and a praise, so that those who go outside, like herdsmen, may know the location of the city; and their name would endure after them all the days of the tower. This is what Scripture said: \"let us make for ourselves a name.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:10.936706407Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}